notes.body:
Does libxml2 construct its entity paths from the path you give it, e.g. would something like

```
getcwd(save_wd, ...);
g_chdir(diameter_dir);
xmlReadFile("./dictionary.xml", ...);
g_chdir(save_wd);
```

work?

It ensures that we pass the relative, ASCII-only portion of the dictionary path to `xmlReadFile`. Assuming that libxml2 doesn't try to convert that to an absolute path, that should avoid any issues with spaces or multibyte character conversion inside the library.

It might be useful to generalize this to a pair of pushd + popd routines in wsutil, e.g.

```
ws_pushd(get_datafile_dir());
xmlReadFile("./dictionary.xml", ...);
ws_popd();
```

and possibly have ws_pushd and ws_popd use GetCurrentDirectory + SetCurrentDirectory on Windows in order to ensure that we properly handle wide paths on that platform.

